00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:36.510
like the visits.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.070
I really enjoy seeing my family.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:38.903
So in prison you could hug them,

00:07:38.903 --> 00:07:40.380
you could see them meet with them.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.937
Whereas in county it's
like through the glass

00:07:41.937 --> 00:07:42.770
and you're like man,

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:43.631
only 20 minutes

00:07:43.631 --> 00:07:45.570
or even 15 for some places.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.613
- I think you should come back over here.

00:07:47.613 --> 00:07:49.037
(guests laugh)

00:07:49.037 --> 00:07:52.370
(Mario mumbles)

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.640
- You know the good thing

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:54.870
about doing time is that your,

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.967
(police siren)

00:07:56.967 --> 00:07:57.800
Your traffic tickets go away.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:58.633
You sign a form.

00:07:58.633 --> 00:07:59.755
(guests laugh)

00:07:59.755 --> 00:08:02.431
- Now, I think you need to come over here.

00:08:02.431 --> 00:08:04.290
- That must be some L.A. stuff.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.490
- You still got your same problem.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:08.107
- I think you should come down.

00:08:08.107 --> 00:08:09.150
Scooch down.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:09.990
- Are we going to switch?

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.009
Are you okay with that?

00:08:11.009 --> 00:08:11.875
All right.

00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:13.110
- And I think for me the
opportunities were there.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.240
To take the classes to better yourself.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.040
But as far as like the treatment goes,

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.470
no, because like the
officers are very indifferent

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.180
so they, they don't treat
you like a human being.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.720
You can't really have a
conversation with them or any staff.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.980
They look at you as less than.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.410
So I felt very dehumanized.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.243
- That's the whole point.

00:08:29.243 --> 00:08:30.076
The whole point of that.

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:30.909
- Okay

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:32.041
Y'all should switch.

00:08:32.041 --> 00:08:34.747
- I feel like you should be over here.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:35.970
- You know, I really,

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.796
I really finessed the
situation when I was in there.

00:08:37.796 --> 00:08:39.720
I know how to work a person.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.553
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.360
My favorite subject is psychology.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.370
- You see everyone
serves time differently.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.616
I didn't do any finessing.

00:08:45.616 --> 00:08:48.843
I was stunned at how many
people didn't do their job.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.600
- It seemed like you
shouldn't even been in prison.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:52.433
- Thank you.

00:08:52.433 --> 00:08:53.341
Thank you.

00:08:53.341 --> 00:08:55.587
- It seemed like you got
caught in a family scheme

00:08:55.587 --> 00:08:57.298
and then they threw you under the bus.

00:08:57.298 --> 00:08:58.249
- A little pyramid scheme.

00:08:58.249 --> 00:08:59.434
- That's what it was.

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:00.540
Your family caught you up

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.070
'cause you just too polished.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:02.913
I can tell.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.616
- I think my mans should be right here

00:09:08.616 --> 00:09:11.070
'cause he been talking
about some in and out.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.080
- I, I know he don't work.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:13.923
- And that he don't work in and out.

00:09:14.776 --> 00:09:15.609
- In-N-Out or in the prison?

00:09:15.609 --> 00:09:16.442
- He wasn't talking
about the burger place.

00:09:16.442 --> 00:09:17.280
when he say In-N-Out.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.777
- I would normally say
American Greed guy should

00:09:19.777 --> 00:09:21.780
be like over here.

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.700
Like you know, Ponzi scheme.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.533
I don't know.

00:09:24.533 --> 00:09:25.740
Yeah, 85%.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.132
- You gonna do most of the time.

00:09:28.132 --> 00:09:29.722
- I mean the Ponzi scheme.

00:09:29.722 --> 00:09:31.406
- Who said Ponzi scheme?

00:09:31.406 --> 00:09:33.000
- You look like a Ponzi scheme.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:33.833
- That's awful.

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:34.920
- I'm not judging you.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.280
- We were doing so well.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.145
- Everyone's been in and out.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.895
(guests chatter)

00:09:48.441 --> 00:09:50.340
- If nothing else, just like you said.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.173
Think about it.

00:09:51.173 --> 00:09:52.530
- Is this the final verdict? Right?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.363
- Fed time.

00:09:53.363 --> 00:09:54.196
- 85%.

00:09:54.196 --> 00:09:55.770
- Fed time, you're going do 80%

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:56.603
or more.

00:09:56.603 --> 00:09:57.436
- I don't think you're number one.

00:09:57.436 --> 00:09:59.040
- No, I don't think I am either.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:01.267
- I would actually maybe
switch you to a two.

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:02.100
- Yeah, I would too.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:02.933
- Yeah.

00:10:02.933 --> 00:10:03.766
- Okay. Okay.

00:10:03.766 --> 00:10:05.250
- Yeah, I like that.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.250
- I agree with that.

00:10:07.374 --> 00:10:10.880
(calm synth-pop music)

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.960
- [Host] For the sixth
spot, we have Mario.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.146
- I told you.

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:16.430
- Wow. I knew it.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:17.263
- Tell you much.

00:10:17.263 --> 00:10:19.374
Are you so serious?

00:10:19.374 --> 00:10:24.230
- [Host] In the fifth spot
we have Nick at one year.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.377
In the fourth spot we have Justin

00:10:26.377 --> 00:10:29.010
at one year and 22 days.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:29.843
- In the Fed's?

00:10:29.843 --> 00:10:31.285
Really?

00:10:31.285 --> 00:10:32.185
- Wow.

00:10:32.185 --> 00:10:33.410
- You should be happy for me.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.320
It could have been worse.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.934
- Yeah, I am for you.

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:36.767
For real.

00:10:36.767 --> 00:10:38.100
Congratulations.

00:10:39.105 --> 00:10:42.968
- [Host] In the third spot we
have Tyrone at three years.

00:10:42.968 --> 00:10:46.584
- Okay. Oh don't tell me
you the bad ass (beep)?

00:10:46.584 --> 00:10:47.597
- I'm not though.

00:10:47.597 --> 00:10:50.033
- [Host] In the second spot
we have Jessica at five years.

00:10:51.645 --> 00:10:52.478
- Oh, yeah.

00:10:52.478 --> 00:10:53.311
Really?

00:10:53.311 --> 00:10:54.144
- Wow.

00:10:54.144 --> 00:10:54.977
- Let me know.

00:10:54.977 --> 00:10:56.485
(Nicholas mumbles).

00:10:56.485 --> 00:10:58.386
- Nail salon?

00:10:58.386 --> 00:11:00.515
- [Host] In the first spot,

00:11:00.515 --> 00:11:02.045
Justin C. At about 14 Years.

00:11:02.045 --> 00:11:03.570
- Damn. My Boy.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.142
- Wow.

00:11:05.142 --> 00:11:06.004
- Whoa.

00:11:06.004 --> 00:11:08.280
- I just didn't get that vibe from him.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.793
- I feel like I don't carry myself

00:11:09.793 --> 00:11:10.680
in a way

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.761
where I'm like a tough guy.

00:11:12.761 --> 00:11:14.490
- You don't even look at him.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.323
- Thank you.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.480
- All right, so I was
on probation for sales.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.190
And then I got caught with weed again.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:26.550
You see back in the days weed was,

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:29.700
you'll get it from somebody's
house, you know, or a corner.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.290
But now you got shops everywhere.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.750
So I got locked up for marijuana.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:34.950
Like plain and simple.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:35.910
- I was a drug dealer.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.470
I was transporting narcotics

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.790
across state lines.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.880
Look and behold I was
part of a sting operation.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:42.930
Didn't know it.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.653
They was surveilling me for like a couple,

00:11:44.653 --> 00:11:46.470
like three days.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:49.230
I plead guilty to 18 months
'cause it was my first charge.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.405
I was in a racist state

00:11:51.405 --> 00:11:53.670
and my judge clearly looked

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.370
at me and told me, 'I'm gonna
make an example outta you

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.020
so I'm gonna send you to prison.'

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.480
- So I pled guilty to
a white collar crime.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.910
One count of conspiracy to commit fraud.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.790
I was a money manager in
Century City at Bear Stearns

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.200
and then UBS.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.260
And many years into my
career our team learned

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.199
that a client of ours
who managed a hedge fund

00:12:12.199 --> 00:12:14.010
was lying to his investors.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.450
Once we learned that he was lying

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.010
rather than stop the fraud,

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:18.270
we turned the other way.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:20.539
In part, 'cause he was paying our company

00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:22.620
100,000 dollars a month,

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.460
every single month.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:25.200
And all of us had grown somewhat addicted

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.550
to the commissions.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.050
Of course, I always knew

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.040
that it was wrong.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.710
And I was certainly deserved
to be held accountable.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:34.004
- My conviction was robbery and possession

00:12:34.004 --> 00:12:35.370
of stolen property.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.840
'Cause I was in gangs.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.570
I was a crip originally
sentenced to seven.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.680
I had a good pd,

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.960
public defender, that
was like you would think

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:43.950
that she was a paid attorney

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.000
the way she fought for me.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.250
And ended up doing three and a half.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.280
- My convictions are
possession with intent,

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:52.320
delivery of meth and
simultaneous possession

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.153
of drugs and a firearm.

00:12:53.153 --> 00:12:55.470
And I was sentenced to
five years in Arkansas.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:56.837
But I also served some other time

00:12:56.837 --> 00:12:58.710
'cause I was a drug addict.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.120
So I have criminal sales

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.640
of a controlled substance
and assault as well.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:06.210
- So I went in for first degree
murder, attempted murder,

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.491
gang related drive-by shooting.

00:13:07.491 --> 00:13:10.312
Something that I'm very remorseful for.

00:13:10.312 --> 00:13:12.330
Because I was born in Korea.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.163
I'm still dealing with the,

00:13:13.163 --> 00:13:15.030
the collateral consequences of it.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:17.700
That I am facing deportation,
that I could literally

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.230
be deported any day.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:21.060
So right now I am pardoning

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.140
or campaigning for my pardon

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:23.640
with the governor of California.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.890
I do believe that I was rightly sentenced

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.110
to 82 years to life.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.570
My sentence was commuted
by the governor down

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:30.720
to 15 years to life.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.800
based on my good behavior.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.110
I went in young, I turned
away from the gangs,

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:34.943
got my GED,

00:13:34.943 --> 00:13:35.790
my college degrees.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.734
So I'm just trying to create
a different narrative.

00:13:37.734 --> 00:13:39.390
And that's the reason why I came on here

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.280
because you know, people do change.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.113
People are not the
horrible choice they made

00:13:42.113 --> 00:13:44.670
as a, as a teenager.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.691
- I'm like you.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:47.182
(Jessica mumbles)

00:13:47.182 --> 00:13:48.015
- [Host] How old are you
When you were sentenced?

00:13:48.015 --> 00:13:48.960
- I was 16?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:49.920
- Your story.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.121
- You see, like this goes to show a lot,

00:13:51.121 --> 00:13:53.280
like if I see anyone of
you guys on the street

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.810
maybe I'll think I'm the bad one.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.391
- But I would think it was you.

00:13:57.391 --> 00:13:58.718
- And maybe me.

00:13:58.718 --> 00:14:01.468
(guests chatter)

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.670
- A lot of times I do sense the fear

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.200
in people when I'm next to them.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.200
But a lot of people that have done

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:13.285
like some of the worst
crimes don't look like me.

00:14:13.285 --> 00:14:15.030
- No, don't judge no one.

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:15.863
For real.

00:14:15.863 --> 00:14:16.696
- Really, I think anyone that's been

00:14:16.696 --> 00:14:19.290
to prison has to work to try
to change that narrative.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.017
Or else everyone in this room
is going to set the narrative

00:14:21.017 --> 00:14:23.400
of how you perceive
people who went to prison.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.420
- That's what we're all are here for.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.770
Just to learn from our mistakes

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:29.763
and become better than
what we were yesterday.

